# Frontend UI Engineering

Build UI that matches the design system and works without a mouse.

## When to use

Creating or changing anything a person sees or operates.

## Process

1. Match the existing component and styling patterns.
2. Handle long text, empty states, and errors.
3. Accessibility is part of done: keyboard access, visible focus, accessible names.
4. Prefer semantic elements over clickable divs.

## Red flags

- Interactive elements with no name and no keyboard path.

## Verification

Local UI patterns are matched and keyboard and empty/error states are covered.
